    "created_at": "2016-04-15T11:41:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-15T11:41:57Z",
    "body": "This is in contrast with what browsers did before they implemented the HTML5 parser: upon reaching an EOF while in a comment, they would rewind the input stream back to `<!--` and parse in a different mode that would close the comment on the first `>`, and then switch to the data state. Since nobody does that anymore, it is academic at this point; we could remove the comment or expand on it, but I don't think it's useful to convert it to a visible note.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
